021 - Immortal, Invisible, God Only Wise
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 21
Topic: Worship - 

Verse 1:
[G]Immortal, [Am/C]invisible, [G]God only [F#dim]wise,
[G]In [C/G]light inaccessible [G]hid from [F#dim]our eyes,
[G/B]Most [Em]blessed, most [D]glorious, [G]the Ancient of days,
[G]Almighty [Am/C]victorious, [G]Thy great name [D7/C]we [G]praise.

Verse 2:
[G]Unresting, [Am/C]unhasting, [G]and silent [F#dim]as light,
[G]Nor [C/G]wanting, [Am/C]nor [D/A]wasting, [G]Thou rulest [F#dim]in might;
[G/B]Thy [Em]justice, [D]like [G/D]mountains, high [Bm/F#]soaring [G]above
[G]Thy [Em]clouds, which [Am/C]are [D/A]fountains [G]of goodness [D7/C]and [G]love.

Verse 3:
[G]To [C/G]all, life [Am/C]Thou [D/A]givest, [G]to both great [F#dim]and small;
[G]In [C/G]all life [Am/C]Thou [D/A]livest, [G]the true life [F#dim]of all;
[G/B]We blossom [Em]and [D]flourish [G]as leaves on the tree,
[G]And [Em]wither [Am/C]and [D/A]perish [G]- but naught changeth Thee.

Verse 4:
[G]Great [C/G]Father [Am/C]of [D/A]glory, [G]pure Father [F#dim]of light,
[G]Thine [C/G]angels [Am/C]adore [D/F#]Thee, [G]all veiling [F#dim]their sight;
[G/B]All [Em]praise we [D]would [G/D]render; O [Bm/F#]help [G]us to see
[G]'Tis [Em]only [Am/C]the [D/A]splendor [G]of light hideth Thee!
